    "description": "Join us on June 4th for the Stripe New York developer meetup. This is an in-person event for anyone building with Stripe. An evening focused on Stripe user experiences, product insights, best practices, and community.\n\n\ud83c\udf55\ud83c\udf81 Perks\nFood and drink provided!\n\n\ud83c\udfab Tickets\nThere is a hard limit for RSVP :) Wait list will be operating on Meetup.\n\n\ud83d\udccdLocation\nThe event is hosted at Stripe's offices.\n\n\ud83d\udd5a Rough timings\n\n6:00 pm - 6:30 pm: Doors open with refreshments\n6:30 pm - 7:45 pm: Talks and Q&A\n7:45 pm - 8:00 pm: Drinks, food, and networking\n\n\ud83d\udce3 Talks\n\n1. **How to Give Agents Spending Power with Privy** **Wallets** \\- Madeleine Charity\\, engineer at Privy\n2. **Building Production-Ready AI Agents with Stripe Projects and Tavily -** Evan Rimer, Forward Deployed Engineer at Tavily\n\nDon't miss this opportunity to connect with the Stripe community.\n\n[Stripe developer code of conduct.](https://stripe.com/legal/developer-code-of-conduct)",
