    "id": "scraped-312-meetup",
    "slug": "veg-night-out-at-rosehill-rooftop-nomadrosehill-meetup-312",
    "orgId": "org-meetup",
    "organizerId": "org-meetup",
    "organizerName": "Meetup Verified Host",
    "organizerColor": "#FF4D4D",
    "title": "Veg Night Out at Rosehill Rooftop (NOMAD/Rosehill)",
    "subtitle": "Curated from Meetup \u00b7 New York",
    "category": "workshop",
    "type": "workshop",
    "tags": [
      "New York",
      "Meetup",
      "Workshop"
    ],
    "description": "Welcome to our monthly Veg Night Out!\n\nThis will be a perfect location for us to chill and enjoy the beautiful summer evening with a panoramic city backdrop. It's an ideal spot for savoring the city's charm with a cocktail in hand as evening falls. Join for a toast to the city that never sleeps.\n\n\"Rosehill Rooftop offers the perfect casual night out with friends, or it gives everyone a reason to snap a few flicks for their follower-filled Instagram feeds\" per **The Mirror US**\n\n**Rosehill Rooftop**\n125 E 27th Street, New York, NY 10016\n917-541-4601\n\n**Supper Magazine:** \"... Positioned at the intersection of uptown and downtown, the venue combines multi-level open-air terraces with indoor lounge spaces, offering unobstructed views of the [Empire State Building](https://www.suppermag.com/tag/new-york/)...\"\n\n**Citi Tour NY** \u201c..With panoramic views, a nod to the city\u2019s storied rooftop tradition, ... Rosehill Rooftop has planted its flag as one of summer\u2019s last must-hit spots ....\u201d\n\nWith all the wonderful vegetarians and vegans who attend each of our events, every event we do is liked by our members, but our \"Veg Night Out!\" events are the most popular of all. People enjoy the fact they can mingle (speak with lots of different people), and they love the beautiful venues that we go to. Join us for a stellar evening of lively conversation and lovely surroundings with fellow vegetarians and vegans.\n\n**For our new members**: this is an incredibly friendly and welcoming group. We'll be hanging out by the main bar area, and you can get to know all our wonderful members.\n\nThis event has no cover and no minimum. But **please do buy a drink or two**, or as many as you like. The venue requests that you dress appropriately: business, business casual or smart casual.\n\nJoin us for a fun and relaxed spring evening socializing with fellow vegetarians and vegans.\n\n**Train Directions**: Take the (6) (R) (1) to 28 St, or the (Path) (F) (M) to 23rd St.\n\nEddie\n\n\\- \\- \\- Vegan / Vegetarian Option \\- \\- \\-\n***Veg Options -*** Please check with staff which can be made vegan\n\\- Blackbird Dip: Avocado\\, black beans\\, roasted corn\\, chunky onion salsa\\, citrus\\, tortilla chips \\(Vegan friendly\\)\n\\- Tacos: Veggie served with avocado mousse\\, salsa ranchera\\, and fresh lime\\.\n\\- French Fries \\(Vegan friendly\\)\n\\- Truffle Parmesan Fries\n\\- Chips & Guacamole: Served with tortilla chips \\(Vegan friendly\\)\n\\- Rosso Pizza \\(Vegan friendly\\)\n\\- Classic Caesa: Baby romaine\\, Caesar dressing\\, garlic croutons\\, parmesan\n\\- Burrata Salad",
