    "description": "**Powering the Next Generation of AI Applications.**\nJoin us on **Saturday, 30th May**, for a deep dive into the systems and hardware orchestration making the AI revolution possible. Hosted at the **Cloudera Bangalore** office in collaboration with **vCluster**, this meetup is designed for engineers, architects, and builders who are navigating the complexities of modern AI stacks.\nFrom the intricacies of **GPU optimization** to the challenges of **scaling inference workloads** on Kubernetes, we are moving beyond the hype and into the \"how-to\" of production AI.\n\n***\n\n### **Event Details**\n\n\ud83d\udcc5 **Date:** Saturday, 30th May 2026\n\ud83d\udd59 **Time:** 10:00 AM \u2013 2:00 PM IST\n\ud83d\udccd **Location:** Cloudera Data Platform India Private LimitedBuilding\nEssae Vaishnavi Summit (4th Floor)Street Address: Number 6/B, 7th Main, 80 Feet Road\nKoramangala Industrial Layout,\nBangalore, Karnataka 560034\n\ud83e\udd1d **Partners:** In collaboration with **vCluster**\n\n### **Agenda**\n\n### **10:00 AM to 10:30 AM**\n\n**Registration & Opening Note**\n\n***\n\n**10:30 AM to 11:00 AM**\n**Talk 1: Building AI Factory,** Speaker: **Saiyam Pathak**\n**About the Speaker:** Saiyam Pathak is the Principal Developer Advocate at Loft Labs and the founder of Kubesimplify, focused on simplifying cloud native and Kubernetes technologies. Previously at Civo, Walmart Labs, Oracle, and HP, he has worked extensively across machine learning platforms, Kubernetes scaling, multi cloud environments, and managed Kubernetes services. Saiyam is also a CNCF TAG Sustainability Lead, community organizer, YouTuber, and open source advocate.\n\n***\n\n**11:00 AM to 11:45 AM**\n**Talk 2: Transitioning from traditional software engineering to AI engineering**\nSpeaker: **Rajesh Kumar and Manas MayankCloudera**\n\n**Summary:** In traditional SWE, you instruct the computer exactly what to do. Since LLMs are inherently unpredictable, in AI Engineering you manage an autonomous reasoning engine by setting boundaries (Guardrails), giving it access to the outside world (Tools/MCP), and heavily monitoring its decision-making process (Evals and Tracing). This talk covers the fundamentals of moving from Software Engineering to AI Engineering.\n\n***\n\n**11:45 AM to 12:15 PM**\n**Talk 3: Inside an AI Factory: GPU Lifecycle, Engineering and the Sovereignty Imperative,** Speaker: **Vijayakumar**\n**About the Speaker:** Vijayakumar is a strategic technology leader and AI executive specializing in enterprise AI infrastructure, cloud platforms, and scalable AI systems. His work at NeevCloud focuses on enabling organizations to operationalize AI securely and efficiently at scale.\n\n***\n\n**12:15 PM to 12:45 PM**\n**Talk 4:** **Identity Propagation in MCP: OBO, Multi-Hop Chains, and the Trust Problem** Speaker: **Ruchika Suryawanshi, Hrittik Roy**\n**About the Speaker:** Ruchika Suryawanshi is a Software Engineer at JPMorganChase and an active contributor to the open source ecosystem. She is passionate about cloud computing, AI, and developer tooling, and has spoken at events including FossAsia and DevConf India. She has also served as a Google Developer Student Club Lead and AI researcher.\n**About the Speaker:** Hrittik Roy is a Platform Advocate at Loft Labs and a CNCF Ambassador with expertise in cloud native technologies and open source communities. He has contributed extensively to developer advocacy, technical writing, and community engagement. Hrittik has spoken at Kubernetes Community Days, Open Source Summits, and multiple cloud native conferences, and has also served on Program Committees for KubeCon and CloudNativeCon events.\n\n***\n\n### **12:45 PM to 01:00 PM**\n\n**Community Activity & Networking**\n\n***\n\n**01:00 PM to 1:30 PM**\n**Talk 5: Engineering Enterprise Serverless Data Agents** Speaker: **Shuva Jyoti Kar**\n**Senior Principal Engineer, Network R&D, Palo Alto Networks**\n**About the Speaker:** Shuva Jyoti Kar is a Senior Principal Engineer at Palo Alto Networks, where he architects secure enterprise AI platforms. He is the author of upcoming books including Engineering the Data Agent Control Plane (O\u2019Reilly) and Agent Skills in Action (Manning). An open source contributor and former OpenDaylight committer, Shuva frequently speaks at Open Source Summit, IEEE conferences, and GDG events on scalable, zero trust AI and data architectures.\n\n***\n\n**1:30 PM to 02:00 PM**\n**Talk 6: From Noisy Logs to Actionable Insights: AI-AssistedObservability with Fluent Bit, OpenSearch & RAG** Speaker: **Jeevitha G**\n**About the Speaker:** Jeevitha G is an Observability Engineer specializing in AI powered monitoring systems built with OpenSearch and cloud native technologies. Her work focuses on transforming high volume logs into actionable insights using Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), Fluent Bit pipelines, and search driven architectures to improve production visibility and incident response.\n\n***\n\n**Who should attend?** Platform Engineers, DevOps/SREs, Data Engineers, AI Researchers, and anyone building the \"plumbing\" that keeps LLMs running.\n\n**Note:** Space is limited to ensure high-quality technical networking. Please Register **[HERE](https://luma.com/xlstctn6)** to secure your spot! Kindly expect a confirmation email post registration to attend.",
