    "description": "Event Agenda and Speaker info\n10:45 - Intro over Tea\n\\-\\-\\- First Half \\-\\-\\-\n11:15 - **AI Ready for SRE: A Practical Maturity Model for Integrating AI into Day-to-Day Operations** - **Zubia Khan & Garima Jangid**, **Google**\nCuts through the AI hype to offer a practical maturity model for SRE. Covers how to make infrastructure \"AI-ready\" to reduce manual toil, build proactive systems, and adapt engineering skillsets for orchestration and safety.\nDuration: 30 mins + Q&A\n\n11:50 - **Beyond Scale: Model Collapse, Diminishing Returns, and the Future of AI** - **Mathangy**, **Western Digital**\nCovers LLMs & SLMs, exploring what happens when scaling hits its limits and what comes next for AI development.\nDuration: 30 mins + Q&A\n\n12:30 - **Lightning Talk** - **Pass Downs from Open Source Summit North America 2026**: Speaker/Attendee Perspective - **Sachin Garg**\nHighlights and takeaways from Open Source Summit NA 2026. (Details TBD)\nDuration: 15 mins + Q&A\n\n1:00 - Lunch\n\n\\-\\-\\- Second Half \\-\\-\\-\n\n2:00 - **Agent Harness Engineering** - **Abhimanyu Shekhawat**, **Google**\nDuration: 30 mins + Q&A\n\n2:35 - **Operational Realities of Autonomous AI Infrastructure**: Reliability, Observability & Scaling Challenges Beyond Traditional Cloud-Native Systems - **SivaKumar G**\\*, **AEITY**\nDuration: 30 mins + Q&A\n\n3:15 - Networking tea and closing",
