    "title": "Introduction to Vibe Sprint",
    "subtitle": "Curated from Meetup \u00b7 Bangalore",
    "category": "hackathon",
    "type": "hackathon",
    "tags": [
      "Bangalore",
      "Meetup",
      "Hackathon"
    ],
    "description": "What if your entire sprint \u2014 from planning to delivery \u2014 was powered by AI agents?\n\nThe Vibe Sprint is a new way to run development sprints where AI agents handle the repetitive work: writing tests, reviewing code, generating documentation, and flagging risks \u2014 while developers focus on architecture and creative problem-solving.\n\nIn this session, you'll see:\n\\- What a Vibe Sprint looks like in practice\n\\- How to set up AI agents for each phase of the sprint\n\\- Real examples of teams shipping faster with fewer developers\n\\- How this fits into existing Agile/Scrum workflows\n\nShort, sharp, and practical. 30 minutes that could change how your team works.\n\n\ud83c\udfa4 Led by a Microsoft Certified Trainer.",
