    "organizerName": "Meetup Verified Host",
    "organizerColor": "#FF4D4D",
    "title": "Global AI Makers Showcase",
    "subtitle": "Curated from Meetup \u00b7 San Francisco",
    "category": "hackathon",
    "type": "hackathon",
    "tags": [
      "San Francisco",
      "Meetup",
      "Hackathon"
    ],
    "description": "**What is this?**\nEvery week, thousands of people build something with AI (an app, an agent, a workflow, an automation) and almost nobody sees it.\n\nAI Makers Global is a live monthly event where the best of those builds get a spotlight.\n\nSubmit what you made. The community votes. The most upvoted submissions get featured live on stream with their creator.\n\nEvery other submission goes into the AI Makers Directory, a permanent public record of what the global AI maker community is building right now.\n\nNo pitch decks. No investor panels. No keynote speakers.\nJust builders showing real things they actually made to the community of AI builders, collaborators, customers, and supporters.\n\n***\n\n**Who should submit?**\nIf you built something with AI in the last 30 days, submit it.\n\nAn app, an agent, a workflow, an automation, a tool, a prototype, a creative project. It doesn't have to be perfect.\n\nIt doesn't have to be a formal company. It just has to be real and live.\nIndie hackers. Founders. Developers. Designers. Operators who automated something at work. Students. People who just started last week. If you made it, we want to see it.\n\n***\n\n**How it works**\n\n**April 23 to May 20: Submit your creation** Fill out the submission form. Tell us what you built, what it does, and drop a link or a short demo video. The form opens one week before the event.\n\n**April 23 to May 20: Community votes** Every submission goes live on the public voting page immediately after you submit. Share your submission with your own audience. The community upvotes what they want to see featured. The top voted submissions get selected for the live show.\n\n**May 22, 11:00 AM CST: The live event**\n11:00 AM: Virtual doors open for the live event. Browse the full submission directory while you wait.\n\n11:10 AM: Welcome from organizer, AI to Done. Why this community exists and what we're building together.\n\n11:15 AM: Featured builds begin. The top upvoted submissions present live. Each creator gets 60 seconds to show what they built. No slides required. Screen share, demo, or just talk through it. Real builds only.\n\n12:00 PM: Open chat round. Remaining submissions shared in the live chat. Host reads and highlights the most interesting ones on stream.\n\n12:15 PM: The AI Makers Directory goes live. Every single submission published at one URL. Permanent. Searchable. Free.\n\n12:20 PM: Close. Next event announced.\n\n***\n\n**The AI Makers Directory**\nEvery submission, featured or not, gets published in the AI Makers Directory after the event at AI to Done. A permanent, searchable, public catalog of what real people built with AI in May 2026.\n\nThink of it as a living document of AI's creative output. Browsable by tool, use case, and builder. Updated after every monthly event.\nIf you want your build discovered by the people who are most curious about what AI can actually do, this is where it lives.\n\n***\n\n**Why watch live?**\nThe directory you can browse any time. The live event you cannot.\nWatching a founder show their build in real time is completely different from reading a product description. You'll see things that aren't in any newsletter. You'll get ideas you wouldn't have had otherwise. And if you have questions, you can ask them live in chat.\n\n***\n\n**Hosted by Kev Page, AI to Done**\nPage has 14 years building community programs for platforms at 1M, 12M, and 100M users. He has helped developer communities grow at PagerDuty, Liquibase, and more.\n\nAI to Done exists to surface the real AI conversation. Not the press releases and predictions. The things people are actually making. Sign-up for the newsletter at\n[aitodone.com](https://aitodone.com)\n\n***\n\n**Time:** 11:00 AM CST / 9:00 AM PT / 12:00 PM ET / 5:00 PM London\n\n**Duration:** 60 minutes\n\n**Cost:** Free\n\n**Location:** Global Live Stream\n\n***\n\n**Register to watch**: Meetup Members can register here.\n\n**Submit your build**: [https://aitodone.com/makers/submit](https://aitodone.com/makers/submit)\n\n**Share this** Know someone building something with AI right now? Send them this. The directory gets more valuable with every submission.",
